end()` to the next newline.\n   - Timings were taken on padme, which shares its cores with other jobs.\n\nThe intent is met otherwise:\n- The round-4 blocker is fixed. In the check, `token=\"FAKEa1\" password=\"FAKEb2\"`, compact JSON with two secret keys, `api_key: \"FAKEa1\" then secret=FAKEb2`, `password='FAKEa1' token=FAKEb2`, three quoted tokens on one line, escaped JSON with two secrets, and the adjacent shapes `token=\"FAKEa1\"password=FAKEb2` and `token=\"\"password=FAKEb2` are all fully redacted.\n- Apart from finding 1, no shape leaks on head that main redacts: the check found 0 new leaks over its 20 shapes. Two shapes that main leaked are now fixed: escaped JSON, and an unterminated quote.\n- Later fields that are not secrets survive: `{\"token\":\"FAKEa1\",\"model\":\"x\",\"password\":\"FAKEb2\"}` gives `{\"<redacted>,\"model\":\"x\",\"<redacted>}`.\n- No pattern can match an empty string, so the search loop cannot spin.\n\nTargeted tests: selected: tests/test_forge_offline.py tests/test_gaze_close.py tests/test_gaze_read_only.py tests/test_gaze_seat.py tests/test_gaze_wall_endpoints.py tests/test_review_panel_cleanup_contract.py; fallback: none; result: pass (6 selected file(s)), 201 passed.\n\nRounds: this is round 5, and blockers keep arriving. Each one has come from how quote structure interacts with the scrub. This one comes from the sequential pattern passes, which the option-C scanner now depends on: an earlier pass can destroy the quotes the scanner needs. Under panel.md \u00a7 Reading the rounds, a fresh blocker this late signals an approach question, not a fix round. Reordering the passes so the key=value pass runs first is the smallest change that removes this class of leak. Whether to apply it or re-ticket is the author's call.\n\nUnresolved simplify: not planned\n\nduration: duration: 3m40s\ntelemetry: wall=na agents=1 tokens=na cost~=$na\nseat: redteam \u00b7 runtime=codex \u00b7 family=openai \u00b7 route=gpt-6.1-sol \u00b7 model=openai/gp